abstract: >-
  Tools for AI-assisted qualitative data coding using large language models
  (LLMs) via the ellmer package, supporting providers including OpenAI,
  Anthropic, Google, Azure, and local models via Ollama. Provides a
  codebook-based workflow for defining coding instructions and applying them
  to texts, images, and other data. Includes built-in codebooks for common
  applications such as sentiment analysis and policy coding, and functions for
  creating custom codebooks for specific research questions. Supports
  systematic replication across models and settings, inter-coder reliability
  statistics, gold-standard validation metrics, and audit trail functionality
  following Lincoln and Guba's (1985) trustworthiness framework.
keywords:
  - R
  - qualitative analysis
  - large language models
  - content analysis
  - text analysis
  - reproducibility
  - qualitative research
